            "accordion_row_wXTFpV": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Why should I use a milk warmer instead of a thermos for formula preparation?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_M7iFtn": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Bottled water has several concerns:Mineral Content: Some have high sodium and sulfate levels, which are not ideal for babies.Sterility: Bottled water is not always sterile, which is critical for newborns.Fluoride Levels: Some contain added fluoride.Temperature Accuracy: The warmer ensures precise temperature control.Microplastics: Bottled water contains more microplastics than tap water.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 20,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_M7iFtn"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_BjyyNT": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "My lid is stuck and won't open. Is it faulty?",
